  "an5.30:0.3": "<p><i>The frame story here is common to three suttas: <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.30'>AN 5:30</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an6.42'>AN 6:42</a>, and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an8.86'>AN 8:103</a>. Although the conversation takes a different turn in each case, in all three cases the Buddha takes the opportunity to teach some unusually plain-spoken truths.</i></p><p>See also: <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn66'>MN 66</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn122'>MN 122</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn17.3'>SN 17:3</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn17.5'>SN 17:5</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn17.8'>SN 17:8</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an4.262'>AN 4:263</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.77'>AN 5:77</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an8.30'>AN 8:30</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an9.40'>AN 9:40</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an10.72'>AN 10:72</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/thag1.86'>Thag 1:86</a></p>",
